      <h1 class="article__title">Can You Trust an AI Chatbot With Schengen Math?</h1>

      <p class="article__meta">October 7, 2026 · 6 min read</p>

      <p class="article__audience">
        <strong>This post is for you if:</strong> you've asked, or are
        thinking of asking, an AI chatbot about your time in the Schengen Area.
        <br />
        <br />
        <strong>It's probably not necessary if:</strong> you just want an
        answer for your own dates. In that case,
        <a href="/app">go straight to the calculator</a>.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="article__body">

      <p>
        During the initial development of EuroVisaCalculator, we found AI chatbots could not be relied upon for rolling window math. 
        This is one of the main reasons why EuroVisaCalculator is AI-free: 
        too often Claude or ChatGPT would provide the wrong answer to a simple question.
      </p>
      <p>
        The state of AI tooling, however, has improved greatly since our initial development, 
        so on October 1st, 2026 we revisited chatbots to see if they'd improved. 
        In this experiment, we asked the free versions of Claude, ChatGPT, and Gemini 20 real
        questions about the Schengen 90/180 rule, then confirmed each answer against the official 
        EU calculator and EuroVisaCalculator, both of which use a purely mathematical calculation.
      </p>

      <nav class="article__toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
        <p class="article__toc-title">On this page</p>
        <ol>
          <li><a href="#results">The short answer</a></li>
          <li><a href="#why-this-happens">Why a wrong answer is easy to believe</a></li>
          <li><a href="#methodology">How we tested</a></li>
          <li><a href="#scenarios">The travelers</a></li>
          <li><a href="#q1">Question 1: When can I return for a full 90 days?</a></li>
          <li><a href="#q2">Question 2: When can I return for a shorter trip?</a></li>
          <li><a href="#q3">Question 3: When do I have to leave?</a></li>
          <li><a href="#q4">Question 4: Can I make this trip?</a></li>
          <li><a href="#q5">Question 5: Coordinating trips</a></li>
          <li><a href="#why-evc">If it's always right, then why not use Claude?</a></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <h2 id="results">The short answer</h2>

      <p>
        Based on these companies' current free tiers, it depends entirely on the chatbot. 
        Claude got all 20 right. 
        ChatGPT and Gemini got 21 of their 40 answers wrong or only partly right.
      </p>

      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table class="scoreboard">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Model</th>
              <th scope="col">✅ Correct</th>
              <th scope="col">🟡 Close</th>
              <th scope="col">❌ Wrong</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th class="vendor-anthropic" scope="row">Claude Sonnet 5.6</th><td>20</td><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr>
            <tr><th class="vendor-openai" scope="row">ChatGPT 5.6 Luna</th><td>13</td><td>1</td><td>6</td></tr>
